class Solution 
 {
  public:
    int reverse(int x) {
        int result = 0;

        while (x != 0) {
            int digit = x % 10;
            x /= 10;

            if (result > INT_MAX / 10 || result < INT_MIN / 10)
                return 0;

            result = result * 10 + digit;
        }

        return result;
    }
};

Explaination:

The code takes the last digit of x using % 10 and adds it to the reversed number. It also checks for 32-bit integer overflow before adding each digit.
